Ongoing work should update the smaller product docs,\ndocs/HARNESS.md:164:stories, durable proof records, and decision records.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-165-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-166-Ongoing work should enter the harness as one of these input types:\ndocs/HARNESS.md-167-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-168-- New spec: a project specification that needs to become product docs and\n--\ndocs/HARNESS.md-171-- Change request: a bounded behavior change, bug fix, or product refinement.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-172-- New initiative: a larger product area that needs multiple stories.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-173-- Maintenance request: dependency, architecture, performance, security, or\ndocs/HARNESS.md-174-  operational work.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:175:- Harness improvement: a process, template, proof, or agent-instruction change.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-176-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-177-The spec-to-work loop is:\ndocs/HARNESS.md-178-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-179-```text\ndocs/HARNESS.md-180-human intent or supplied spec\ndocs/HARNESS.md-181-  -> classify input type\ndocs/HARNESS.md-182-  -> update or create product contract\ndocs/HARNESS.md-183-  -> create story packet or initiative notes when needed\ndocs/HARNESS.md:184:  -> define validation proof\ndocs/HARNESS.md-185-  -> implement or document the blocker\ndocs/HARNESS.md:186:  -> update product docs, stories, durable proof records, and decisions\ndocs/HARNESS.md-187-  -> capture harness friction\ndocs/HARNESS.md-188-```\ndocs/HARNESS.md-189-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-190-Large product areas should use scoped initiative notes instead of a second\ndocs/HARNESS.md-191-monolithic specification. An initiative should explain the goal, affected\ndocs/HARNESS.md:192:product docs, candidate stories, validation shape, open decisions, and exit\ndocs/HARNESS.md-193-criteria. If initiative work becomes a repeated pattern, add a template or\ndocs/HARNESS.md-194-record the proposal with `scripts/bin/harness-cli backlog add`.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-195-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-196-## Growth Rule\ndocs/HARNESS.md-197-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-198-The harness grows from friction.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-199-\ndocs/HARNESS.md:200:When an agent is confused, repeats manual reasoning, needs a new validation\ndocs/HARNESS.md-201-command, discovers a missing rule, or sees a recurring failure pattern, it must\ndocs/HARNESS.md-202-either improve the harness directly or record the friction:\ndocs/HARNESS.md-203-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-204-```bash\ndocs/HARNESS.md-205-scripts/bin/harness-cli backlog add --title \"<short name>\" --pain \"<what was hard>\"\ndocs/HARNESS.md-206-```\ndocs/HARNESS.md-207-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-208-Use the backlog outcome loop for improvements that are expected to change agent\ndocs/HARNESS.md:209:behavior or validation results:\ndocs/HARNESS.md-210-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-211-1. When creating the backlog item, fill `--predicted` with the measurable\ndocs/HARNESS.md-212-   impact expected from the improvement.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-213-2. When closing the item, fill `--outcome` with the actual measured result or\n--\ndocs/HARNESS.md-253-1. Bootstrap the local ignored runtime with `scripts/bootstrap-harness.sh` on\ndocs/HARNESS.md-254-   macOS/Linux or `.\\scripts\\bootstrap-harness.ps1` on Windows.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-255-2. Classify the request with `docs/FEATURE_INTAKE.md` and record the\ndocs/HARNESS.md-256-   classification with `scripts/bin/harness-cli intake`.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:257:3. Check focused proof status with\ndocs/HARNESS.md-258-   `scripts/bin/harness-cli query matrix --active --summary`, then use\ndocs/HARNESS.md-259-   `scripts/bin/harness-cli query matrix --story <id>` if a story is selected.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-260-4. Retrieve only the affected product, story, decision, and implementation\ndocs/HARNESS.md-261-   files required by the selected lane in `docs/CONTEXT_RULES.md`.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:262:5. Implement and validate inside that lane: tiny, normal, or high-risk.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:263:6. Before finishing, ask whether product truth, validation expectations,\ndocs/HARNESS.md-264-   architecture rules, repeated failure patterns, or next-agent instructions\ndocs/HARNESS.md-265-   changed.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-266-7. Record a trace with `scripts/bin/harness-cli trace`, using\ndocs/HARNESS.md-267-   `docs/TRACE_SPEC.md` for the expected trace tier and field depth, and review\n--\ndocs/HARNESS.md-270-   `scripts/bin/harness-cli backlog add`.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-271-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-272-## Story Verification\ndocs/HARNESS.md-273-\ndocs/HARNESS.md:274:Stories may carry a mechanical proof command:\ndocs/HARNESS.md-275-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-276-```bash\ndocs/HARNESS.md-277-scripts/bin/harness-cli story add --id US-012 --title \"Story verification\" --lane normal --verify \"cargo test --workspace\"\ndocs/HARNESS.md-278-scripts/bin/harness-cli story update --id US-012 --verify \"cargo test --workspace\"\n--\ndocs/HARNESS.md-289-skips stories without `verify_command`, and exits 1 if any configured story\ndocs/HARNESS.md-290-fails.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-291-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-292-`story verify` accepts only the story id. Configure the command with\ndocs/HARNESS.md:293:`story add --verify` or `story update --verify`. Record proof booleans with\ndocs/HARNESS.md-294-`story update`, using numeric values: `1` means yes and `0` means no. The Rust\ndocs/HARNESS.md-295-CLI rejects text values such as `yes` and `no`.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-296-\ndocs/HARNESS.md:297:Use `scripts/bin/harness-cli query matrix --numeric` when copying proof values\ndocs/HARNESS.md-298-back into `story update`. The default matrix output is human-readable\ndocs/HARNESS.md-299-`yes`/`no`; the numeric output mirrors CLI input.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-300-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-301-Use `query matrix --active --summary` to omit completed history and long\ndocs/HARNESS.md:302:evidence text while retaining lane, runnable state, and proof columns.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-303-`--runnable` uses the same planned/nonblank-verification/unblocked rule as\ndocs/HARNESS.md-304-protocol story discovery, and `--story <id>` selects one exact story. Filters\ndocs/HARNESS.md-305-combine with AND semantics. The unfiltered matrix remains the full durable\ndocs/HARNESS.md:306:proof view.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-307-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-308-`story complete <id>` is the explicit lifecycle transition for completed work.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:309:It requires an `in_progress` or `changed` story, runs fresh proof, and marks the\ndocs/HARNESS.md:310:story implemented only when that proof passes. Resolver stories additionally\ndocs/HARNESS.md-311-require a stable linked Harness-improvement intake and a completed matching\ndocs/HARNESS.md-312-implementation trace recorded after the newest resolver link. On pass, story\ndocs/HARNESS.md:313:proof and eligible accepted backlog closures are committed atomically and\ndocs/HARNESS.md-314-replayably. Ordinary text updates and JSON compare-and-set updates reject an\ndocs/HARNESS.md-315-`implemented` target and direct the caller to `story complete`; other lifecycle,\ndocs/HARNESS.md:316:proof, evidence, and verification-command updates remain available. Ordinary\ndocs/HARNESS.md:317:`story verify` and `story verify-all` remain proof-only.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-318-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-319-## Phase 5 Evolution Commands\ndocs/HARNESS.md-320-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-321-Tool discovery:\n--\ndocs/HARNESS.md-325-scripts/bin/harness-cli query tools --json\ndocs/HARNESS.md-326-scripts/bin/harness-cli tool register --name <name> --command <cmd> --description <text> --responsibility Verification\ndocs/HARNESS.md-327-```\ndocs/HARNESS.md-328-\ndocs/HARNESS.md:329:Context and drift checks:\ndocs/HARNESS.md-330-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-331-```bash\ndocs/HARNESS.md-332-scripts/bin/harness-cli score-context <trace-id>\ndocs/HARNESS.md-333-scripts/bin/harness-cli audit\n--\ndocs/HARNESS.md-364-## Decision Records\ndocs/HARNESS.md-365-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-366-High-risk work needs durable decisions when it changes behavior or architecture.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-367-For auth, authorization, data ownership, API shape, audit/security, or\ndocs/HARNESS.md:368:validation changes, record the decision in both places:\ndocs/HARNESS.md-369-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-370-1. Add a markdown file under `docs/decisions/` from\ndocs/HARNESS.md-371-   `docs/templates/decision.md`.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-372-2. Add or refresh the durable record:\n--\ndocs/HARNESS.md-389-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-390-- Non-completion story status and evidence via\ndocs/HARNESS.md-391-  `scripts/bin/harness-cli story update`; use `story complete` to reach\ndocs/HARNESS.md-392-  `implemented`.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:393:- Test matrix rows via `scripts/bin/harness-cli story add` and\ndocs/HARNESS.md-394-  `scripts/bin/harness-cli story update`.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-395-- Links from story packets to product docs.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:396:- Validation notes and reports.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-397-- Small clarifications tied to the current task.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-398-- Intake records, traces, and backlog items via `scripts/bin/harness-cli`.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-399-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-400-Agents should ask for human confirmation before:\ndocs/HARNESS.md-401-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-402-- Changing architecture direction.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:403:- Removing validation requirements.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-404-- Changing the source-of-truth hierarchy.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-405-- Changing risk classification rules.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-406-- Replacing the feature workflow.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-407-\n--\ndocs/HARNESS.md-413-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-414-A change request is done only when:\ndocs/HARNESS.md-415-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-416-- The requested change is completed or the blocker is documented.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:417:- Relevant docs, stories, and test matrix entries remain current.\ndocs/HARNESS.md:418:- Validation commands were run when they exist.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-419-- A trace has been recorded with `scripts/bin/harness-cli trace`.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-420-- Missing Harness capabilities were recorded with\ndocs/HARNESS.md-421-  `scripts/bin/harness-cli backlog add` when relevant.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-422-- The final response says what changed and what was not attempted.\ndocs/HARNESS.md-423-\ndocs/HARNESS.md:424:## Future Validation Ladder\ndocs/HARNESS.md-425-\ndocs/HARNESS.md:426:No validation scripts exist yet. When implementation begins, the expected ladder\ndocs/HARNESS.md-427-is:\ndocs/HARNESS.md-428-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-429-```text\ndocs/HARNESS.md:430:validate:quick\ndocs/HARNESS.md:431:  format, lint, typecheck, unit tests, architecture check\ndocs/HARNESS.md-432-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-433-test:integration\ndocs/HARNESS.md:434:  backend, database, provider, or service checks as the stack requires\ndocs/HARNESS.md-435-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-436-test:e2e\ndocs/HARNESS.md-437-  user-visible end-to-end flows\ndocs/HARNESS.md-438-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-439-test:platform\ndocs/HARNESS.md:440:  shell, mobile, desktop, or deployment smoke checks as the stack requires\ndocs/HARNESS.md-441-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-442-test:release\ndocs/HARNESS.md:443:  full suite, log checks, and performance smoke\ndocs/HARNESS.md-444-```\ndocs/HARNESS.md-445-\ndocs/HARNESS.md-446-Agents must not claim these commands pass until they exist and have been run.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
