{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n -i -C 4 \"validate|unit|check-local|local\" README.md scripts/README.md'","aggregated_output":"scripts/README.md-12-diagnose, plan, and status requests remain read-only: inspect what is already\nscripts/README.md-13-present, and do not bootstrap, initialize/migrate, record intake, or trace.\nscripts/README.md-14-\nscripts/README.md-15-For a change, build, or fix request after a fresh clone or install, bootstrap\nscripts/README.md:16:the local ignored runtime before querying or changing state:\nscripts/README.md-17-\nscripts/README.md-18-```bash\nscripts/README.md-19-scripts/bootstrap-harness.sh\nscripts/README.md-20-```\n--\nscripts/README.md-27-source so code and command behavior cannot drift. It refuses to invent an empty\nscripts/README.md-28-replacement when the default core database is missing, and it rejects a\nscripts/README.md-29-schema-current database that still contains product-owned state. Restore the\nscripts/README.md-30-verified core epoch in that case. In an installed consumer it uses the\nscripts/README.md:31:checksum-verified prebuilt binary and safely initializes a missing local\nscripts/README.md-32-database. Both modes migrate older supported databases and refuse unsupported\nscripts/README.md-33-schemas or CLI/release-pin drift.\nscripts/README.md-34-\nscripts/README.md-35-```bash\nscripts/README.md-36-scripts/bin/harness-cli init          # Create the database\nscripts/README.md-37-scripts/bin/harness-cli intake ...    # Record a feature intake classification\nscripts/README.md-38-scripts/bin/harness-cli story ...     # Add or update a story (test matrix row)\nscripts/README.md:39:scripts/bin/harness-cli story update --id US-001 --unit 1 --integration 1 --e2e 0 --platform 0\nscripts/README.md-40-scripts/bin/harness-cli story verify US-001  # Run the story's verify_command\nscripts/README.md-41-scripts/bin/harness-cli story complete US-001 # Fresh proof plus atomic lifecycle completion\nscripts/README.md-42-scripts/bin/harness-cli decision ...  # Add a decision or run its verification\nscripts/README.md-43-scripts/bin/harness-cli backlog ...   # Add or close a backlog item\n--\nscripts/README.md-216-A source branch can pin the release used by the installer through\nscripts/README.md-217-`scripts/harness-cli-release-tag`; Phase 3 pins `harness-cli-v0.1.4` so branch\nscripts/README.md-218-installs receive a Phase 3-built CLI. Set `HARNESS_CLI_RELEASE_TAG` to override\nscripts/README.md-219-that tag, or set `HARNESS_CLI_BASE_URL` to point at an alternate artifact\nscripts/README.md:220:directory, such as a local `file:///.../dist` directory created by\nscripts/README.md-221-`scripts/build-harness-cli-release.sh`.\nscripts/README.md-222-\nscripts/README.md-223-`--merge` (PowerShell: `-Merge`) deliberately does not replace an existing CLI.\nscripts/README.md-224-To upgrade a CLI explicitly, pin one immutable tag for both the template files\n--\nscripts/README.md-254-\nscripts/README.md-255-Repository maintainers and pull-request CI run the same release-relevant gate:\nscripts/README.md-256-\nscripts/README.md-257-```bash\nscripts/README.md:258:scripts/validate-premerge.sh\nscripts/README.md-259-```\nscripts/README.md-260-\nscripts/README.md-261-It checks Rust formatting, tests, and linting; revision/schema/command\nscripts/README.md-262-coherence; bootstrap, protocol, installer, documentation, and representative\n--\nscripts/README.md-268-\nscripts/README.md-269-Run the durable repository rebuild and its validator contract regressions:\nscripts/README.md-270-\nscripts/README.md-271-```bash\nscripts/README.md:272:scripts/validate-changeset-rebuild.sh\nscripts/README.md:273:scripts/test-validate-changeset-rebuild.sh\nscripts/README.md-274-```\nscripts/README.md-275-\nscripts/README.md-276-The validator builds the current workspace CLI unless `HARNESS_CLI` is set\nscripts/README.md-277-explicitly. `HARNESS_CHANGESET_DIR` can point validation at a copied fixture\n--\nREADME.md-44-- What decision or lesson should future agents inherit?\nREADME.md-45-\nREADME.md-46-In this repo, those answers live in:\nREADME.md-47-\nREADME.md:48:- `AGENTS.md` — the stable agent shim with local project notes and Harness\nREADME.md-49-  doc links.\nREADME.md-50-- `docs/HARNESS.md` — the human-agent collaboration model.\nREADME.md-51-- `docs/FEATURE_INTAKE.md` — tiny, normal, and high-risk work classification.\nREADME.md-52-- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — architecture discovery and boundary rules.\n--\nREADME.md-106-\nREADME.md-107-The refresh backs up the existing file. If it detects the old\nREADME.md-108-Harness-generated guide, it replaces it with the shim. If the file appears\nREADME.md-109-custom, it appends or updates a marked Harness block instead of overwriting the\nREADME.md:110:project's local instructions.\nREADME.md-111-\nREADME.md-112-If the project is driven with Claude Code, add `--claude`. Claude Code never\nREADME.md-113-auto-loads `AGENTS.md`, so without this the installed harness is invisible to\nREADME.md-114-fresh sessions. The flag installs (or refreshes) a `CLAUDE.md` whose marked\n--\nREADME.md-137-verifies its `.sha256` checksum, and installs it at\nREADME.md-138-`scripts/bin/harness-cli` on macOS/Linux or `scripts/bin/harness-cli.exe` on\nREADME.md-139-Windows. The Rust CLI is the main Harness tool and stable command path.\nREADME.md-140-\nREADME.md:141:Then bootstrap the local ignored database. A Harness source checkout builds the\nREADME.md:142:CLI from that checkout and validates the restored core-state epoch; it refuses\nREADME.md-143-to fabricate an empty replacement for missing repository state. An installed\nREADME.md:144:project reuses the verified release binary and initializes its own empty local\nREADME.md-145-state:\nREADME.md-146-\nREADME.md-147-```bash\nREADME.md-148-scripts/bootstrap-harness.sh\n--\nREADME.md-228-\nREADME.md-229-Installing Harness into another repository does not create or choose that\nREADME.md-230-consumer's application, stack, or product specification. It adds the reusable\nREADME.md-231-engineering layer that helps humans and agents turn the consumer's intent into\nREADME.md:232:validated work.\nREADME.md-233-\nREADME.md-234-## Product Sources\nREADME.md-235-\nREADME.md-236-The upstream Harness contract lives in this README, the operating documents,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
